{
  "notes": [
    "Golden vectors for the stored meta 0x02 entries of a client-chunked fetch. The contract is docs/specs/client-chunked-fetch.md in entiredb. Generator: internal/xet/fetch_vectors_test.go.",
    "input names an input of client_vectors.json. Each xorb of an entry is a xorb of that file: an input xorb, or the new xorb of the dedup entry for the same input. A client can rebuild the input from them.",
    "Xet hashes (file, xorb) are in Xet text form, as in client_vectors.json. Entry hex holds the raw 32 bytes.",
    "entries: complete stored pack entries (type 5 header with the logical size, meta byte 0x02, payload size uvarint, payload) and their parsed fields. The payload is the blob OID, the file hash, the xorb count and hashes, the term count, and six uvarints for each term: xorb index, chunk start, chunk end (half-open), unpacked bytes, first byte, last byte.",
    "first_byte and last_byte are the inclusive range of the term's chunks in the stored xorb: first_byte is the stored end of chunk chunk_start-1 (0 for chunk 0), and last_byte is the stored end of chunk chunk_end-1, minus 1. Stored ends are the stored_ends of the xorb in client_vectors.json.",
    "Recipe \"xorbs of the input\" has one term for each input xorb. Recipe \"dedup against <base>\" is the recipe of the client entry of the same name in client_vectors.json, with byte ranges.",
    "invalid_entries: complete entries that entiredb refuses as a stored chunked entry. error is a substring of entiredb's error text. A client refuses each of them too."
  ],
